  </model>
  <!-- Marker dropping. Two bins, distinguished by a white symbol painted
       on the floor of each: a ring ("O") at x=3.6 and a cross ("X") at
       x=4.6, both at y=-4.0.

       Without these the two bins were geometrically identical navy boxes
       and the O/X only existed in the link names, so the classification
       step had nothing to see.

       The symbols are deliberately built so that TWO independent cues
       separate them, which makes the classifier hard to fool in murky
       water:
         - circularity: the disc of the ring nearly fills its enclosing
           circle, the cross fills about a third of its own
         - topology: the ring is drawn as a white disc with a navy plug
           on top, so it renders as an annulus and its contour has a
           child. The cross has none. That is the same inner-contour
           trick the heart cutout will need later.

       Symbols sit at z=0.025..0.032, just proud of the 0.02 thick floor,
       so they cannot z-fight with it. -->
